EXT. AUTO SALVAGE YARD - CAR CRUSHER BAY - NIGHT

Towers of flattened cars. A hydraulic crusher squats at the end of a gravel lane, its steel jaws open like a mouth. A sodium lamp buzzes on a pole.

A MAN in a dark jacket, 40s, slams the trunk of a black sedan shut. He wipes his hands on his pants. From the passenger side, a WOMAN in a leather coat, 30s, hurries around the car, hugging herself.

At the office window, a KID, 17, in a hoodie, watches from behind a curtain.

The man opens the sedan's back door. A heavy gym bag sits on the seat.

WOMAN
Did you check the plates?

MAN
Twice.

WOMAN
Did you check the plates again?

MAN
Nina. They're clean.

WOMAN
(softly)
Don't say my name.

MAN
Who's going to hear?

She nods toward the office. The Kid has vanished from the window.

MAN (CONT'D)
That's Terrence's nephew. He doesn't count.

NINA
Everyone counts.

The man hauls out the gym bag. It lands on the gravel with a clink.

The office door opens. The Kid steps out, hands in pockets, walking slow.

KID
You guys need the crusher?

MAN
Yeah. For the sedan.

KID
Papers?

NINA
No papers.

KID
No papers, no crusher. That's Terrence's rule.

MAN
Terrence is a friend.

KID
Terrence is in Phoenix.

The man smiles, shows teeth. He steps closer. The Kid doesn't step back.

MAN
Kid. What's your name?

KID
Eli.

MAN
Eli. Listen to me. A man left this car here. It's got to go.

ELI
Then he can come back and fill out a form.

NINA
Eli, we're running behind.

ELI
Then you should've been on time.

The man lunges, grabs Eli by the hoodie. Eli drops his phone, kicks the man's shin, and twists free. The man staggers into the sedan's open door. Nina grabs the gym bag and swings it into the man's back. All three go down in the gravel, tangled.

Eli scrambles to the crusher's control panel. Slaps a lever. The jaws groan and begin to close.

NINA
Eli! Don't!

ELI
(shouting)
You said no papers!

The man rolls away. The jaws descend on the sedan with a scream of metal. The gym bag, caught half under the door, is dragged in.

Nina stares, mouth open. The man gets up slowly, face bleeding.

MAN
(to Eli, hoarse)
You have any idea what was in that bag?

ELI
(dead calm)
Terrence's rules.

The crusher bottoms out. Glass bursts. A cloud of dust and loose banknotes swirls up through the sodium light, drifting down like snow.
